From abc9f17b3f4c92fdcc94f271002390a8f2f32ad9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:49:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Underlying-first measurement for swings and 0DTE: bar-based
 references, stop/target path, cell switches

Rebased onto main be6405b (whole-list 0DTE book + swings retirement).
Both option books scored only the option quote path, so an observation
existed only when a streamed contract quote arrived in time (swings: 127
tickets, 0 conversions; 0DTE: 11,311 tickets, 30 observed). The signal was
never measured in production. This scores every candidate on the underlying
from stored 1-minute bars, independent of option quotes:

- compass/underlying_path.py: pure helpers (next-bar entry, horizon returns,
  stop-first bracket with gap fills, bar-close reference at a target).
- swing_study: register candidates without a 5 s quote using the signal bar
  close (entry_source), checkpoint fallback to the completed bar close
  (bar_close_reference), first_of_day flag, score_path writes the production
  stop/2R/10-session path as underlying_path when the 9-session checkpoint
  resolves; report aggregates it by rule x side (all fires / first of day).
- scanner_shadow.score_underlying: every seated or shadow 0DTE record, quoted
  or data_gap, gets +30/+60/+120/flatten bps and the invalidation/2R bracket
  once the session ends; scorecard cells carry the summary beside Quill's
  closed-record _crosscheck (kept; complementary).
- SWING_RULES / SWING_SIDES switches (defaults unchanged: every cell on;
  SWING_IDEAS_ENABLED itself stays at Josh's retired default).

No seat, allowlist, booking, alert or premium-P&L behaviour changes.
Evidence: claude-exchange/from-claude/2026-11-01-swings-0dte.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012WE3e5zGd83u4HvstL2kcs
